WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:07.000
Good morning and welcome to what I eat in a day.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.500
Today, I'm going to show you everything I eat,

3
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.400
and we're going to learn some English about food.

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.300
We're going to learn some really common food English,

5
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.000
and you're going to learn it in a really good, easy way,

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.000
because I'm just going to vlog what I eat today.

7
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.800
So, let's start with breakfast,

8
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.000
the most important meal of the day.

9
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.500
So, I'm actually a bit of a creature of habit.

10
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.500
I really like having very similar food most days.

11
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.500
So, this is the breakfast I have every single day,

12
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.400
and I don't get bored of it.

13
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.500
So, we've got Greek yogurt.

14
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.300
I'm going to do Greek yogurt with almond butter.

15
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.600
Ooh, I love almond butter. Let me show you.

16
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:57.600
We're going to have...

17
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.200
Disaster. Oh no,

18
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.500
that is not what I wanted at all. Gosh.

19
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.500
Oh no, I fully split it all.

20
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.500
To start my day then, I'm just going to transfer all this Greek yogurt into this.

21
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:17.300
Bear with me a second. Promise we'll get to a what I eat in a day video very shortly.

22
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.000
I'm very clumsy.

23
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.800
If that didn't show you that I'm a clumsy person, I don't know what will.

24
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:28.300
I have no coordination. I often drop things. Very, very clumsy.

25
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:36.300
Okay, so that wasn't quite the glamorous opening of a video I wanted,

26
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:37.800
but that's fine.

27
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:44.000
So, what I normally do for breakfast is I normally get a bowl.

28
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.000
Watch out for the pronunciation of that word, by the way.

29
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Bowl, not bowel. Very different thing.

30
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.000
And then I still have a little bit of yogurt in this one.

31
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.000
So, I get some Greek yogurt in a bowl.

32
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:04.000
I just like Greek yogurt because it's very filling.

33
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.300
It's very filling. It keeps me full for a long time.

34
00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.000
And I think that's what you want with breakfast.

35
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.500
You want... you want to feel full for a long time.

36
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:22.300
I don't want to eat breakfast, and then two seconds later, oh, I'm hungry again.

37
00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:25.100
So, I have my Greek yogurt in a bowl.

38
00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:31.800
Um, it doesn't look very appetizing right now, but I need an apple, and I also need some almond butter.

39
00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:39.800
So, I get a good scoop of almond butter. And I normally... So, I add that in there.

40
00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.200
Then I mix it all in there. Mix, mix, mix, mix, mix.

41
00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:50.300
Then I chop the apple up. I chop it up, or I cut the apple into smaller pieces,

42
00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:57.200
or I cut the apple into chunks.

43
00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:00.100
So we can often talk about food in chunks.

44
00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:04.600
So a chunk is a non-specified measurement.

45
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:09.900
I'm not... I'm not measuring these. That's just a chunk of apple, you know.

46
00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:15.000
Uh, and I don't use the core of the apple. I don't need the core.

47
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.000
I don't want the seeds. Or in the UK, we call seeds "pips".

48
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.100
I don't know whether that's just a UK thing, but when I was younger,

49
00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.400
I would always say, "Ooh, mom, I want an orange,

50
00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.600
but I don't want an orange with any pips in it."

51
00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:32.800
Then I mix all that together so that the apple is evenly spread throughout the thing.

52
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:38.300
And then to finish it off, I just top it with some blueberries.

53
00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:41.000
Sprinkle some blueberries on the top.

54
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.500
Easy peasy lemon squeezy. Let's go eat it.

55
00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:50.800
Oh, I need a coffee. I haven't made myself a coffee.

56
00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:54.000
Clearly the yogurt just threw me off.

57
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.000
We've decorated for Christmas, which is very exciting.

58
00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:01.300
Um, but yes, so I've got my Greek yogurt bowl with my blueberries.

59
00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:06.800
Tuck in.

60
00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:11.000
Okay, it's now later in the day. It's time for lunch.

61
00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.800
I really enjoy lunch. Most weekdays I just have a salad.

62
00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.800
It's really, really boring.

63
00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.700
But it's a Saturday, so I'm going to have possibly one of my favorite foods ever.

64
00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:22.500
Let me show you.

65
00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:28.500
I'm actually really excited for this because it's the beginning of the Christmas season.

66
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:36.500
So now I have complete free rein to eat as much turkey and cranberry sauce as I want.

67
00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:41.200
That is my favorite combination of anything.

68
00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:45.000
In the UK in particular, Christmas dinner involves a turkey.

69
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:50.100
Big turkey with cranberry sauce and gravy.

70
00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:55.000
It is phenomenal. That mixture of savory with sweet. I just love it.

71
00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:59.500
I've always liked having, like, meat and then a sweet sauce on it.

72
00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:05.400
So, like, duck in orange sauce, chicken in lemon sauce, you know, that combination.

73
00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:11.000
So I'm going to make a bagel with turkey, butter, and cranberry sauce.

74
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:15.500
It's really simple, but I think it might be my favorite food of all time.

75
00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:19.500
Okay, so I'm going to make my bagel. I'm going to toast my bagel.

76
00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:25.500
These are the protein bagels. They've got seeds on them. I just like it.

77
00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:30.000
So, I'm going to toast these, put some turkey in it, and then put some cranberry sauce on it.

78
00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.400
Oh my goodness. Take a look, by the way, at my butter dish.

79
00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.800
How sweet is this butter dish?

80
00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.600
I'm just... I...

81
00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:42.100
Little things like this bring me so much joy.

82
00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:46.400
So, this is my butter dish, and inside we have some butter.

83
00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:54.400
Obviously, I know it might seem really simple and silly, but a turkey bagel with cranberry sauce.

84
00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:08.900
I can eat this every day for the rest of my life and I'll be happy.
